cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or review this work, please cite it as below, together with the exact release or commit used."
type: software
title: "Ordered-weight certificates for odd cycles in dense coprime graphs: A computer-assisted argument for Erdős Problem 883(i)"
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/wizardscurtain/erdos-883-ordered-weight-proof"
url: "https://github.com/wizardscurtain/erdos-883-ordered-weight-proof"
abstract: >-
  A computer-assisted proof that if A is a subset of {1,...,n} with
  |A| > floor(n/2) + floor(n/3) - floor(n/6), then the coprime graph on A
  contains a cycle of every odd length L with 3 <= L <= floor(n/3) + 1, for
  every n (Erdős Problem 883, part (i)). Uses adjusted totient weights, an
  ordered Hall/connector argument, analytic bounds for n >= 10^8, and
  arithmetic and LRAT-checked SAT certificates below that.
authors:
